# CMS embed CSS

WordPress / Elementor themes ship unlayered `button`, `input`, `table`, and heading rules. Those beat Tailwind's `@layer` output regardless of specificity.

- Scope finished CSS with `scripts/postcss-scope-embed.cjs` in each widget `inline-css.cjs` and in App Manager `prepare-shared-css.cjs`.
- Scope product-page `shared.css` to every non-standalone app id in `studio.config.json`, plus `${id}-portal`.
- Import `src/styles/host-reset.css`. Portal with `portalRoot(containerId)`, not `document.body`.
- Publish `shared.css` only. Never emit or copy `bp-shared.css`.
- `@import "tailwindcss" important` does not replace the PostCSS unlayer step.

See `docs/CMS-EMBED-CSS.md`.
